From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thisiscamk <100883750+thisiscamk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: rtkit: Map app endpoints from the epmap_done
 callback

A driver with an epmap_done callback starts its app endpoint before the
co-processor reaches the running state, but apple_rtkit_app_ep_to_ep()
only answers once it runs, so such a driver has to hardcode where the
app endpoints start, which differs between protocol versions.

Answer for these drivers as soon as the protocol is negotiated. Drivers
without the callback see no change.

[Orchard: from thisiscamk/ipad-air-j72-linux 2a257d6,
 code/current/kernel/0001-j72-installed-kernel-snapshot.patch: his ASP
 driver picks the storage endpoint from the negotiated protocol through
 a new apple_rtkit_protocol_version() export; reworked to answer through
 the existing app endpoint helper instead.]
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c       | 7 ++++++-
 include/linux/soc/apple/rtkit.h | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c b/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c
index 521c7b234..b54688f56 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c
@@ -972,7 +972,12 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_rtkit_poweroff);
 
 u8 apple_rtkit_app_ep_to_ep(struct apple_rtkit *rtk, u8 app_ep)
 {
-	if (!apple_rtkit_is_running(rtk))
+	/*
+	 * The app endpoints are known once the protocol is negotiated, which
+	 * a driver with an epmap_done callback needs before power-on.
+	 */
+	if (!apple_rtkit_is_running(rtk) &&
+	    !(rtk->ops->epmap_done && rtk->version))
 		return 0;
 
 	return rtk->app_ep_start + app_ep;
diff --git a/include/linux/soc/apple/rtkit.h b/include/linux/soc/apple/rtkit.h
index ef33268f3..3c17d415e 100644
--- a/include/linux/soc/apple/rtkit.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/apple/rtkit.h
@@ -195,7 +195,9 @@ int apple_rtkit_poll(struct apple_rtkit *rtk);
  * Convert an endpoint number relative to start of app endpoint to an absolute
  * endpoint number.
  *
- * Returns the endpoint number on success, 0 on failure.
+ * Returns the endpoint number on success, 0 on failure. A driver with an
+ * epmap_done callback may call it from that callback; others only once the
+ * co-processor runs.
  *
  * @rtk:            RTKit reference
  */
